[EXPLAIN] What this step does
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  The MoleculeACE targets were run one at a time under the 'generalization' profile (steps 01 and
  09, 5x1 folds),         and once more on the published 80/20 partition (step 21). Each target
  gives a paired comparison of its own; this         step treats the targets as the units of a
  second-level test: does the classical advantage hold across targets,         on the published
  split, and on its activity cliffs? Where step 12 (the D-MPNN with a nested hyperparameter
  search) was run, it also reports whether tuning closes the gap.
